[{:db/id "q-336533/selection/9111e286e028a3b1572db98fcd1243c12bef07f305596b311cec8f8a0f454bc2" :answer/id #uuid "aa70ffd8-c368-54c6-81f7-26dbe8b7688e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+4I=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533/selection/c6e9e1786651e68e47bfd6d8dfa488215d83d8471885336cc662bd783796c744" :answer/id #uuid "df48ce28-d9cf-59cb-adee-f47165ef989f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-18I=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533/selection/b584697703567f8b802de003bcc741885eed27ee25f4f9483d253ce765801b6c" :answer/id #uuid "2621019d-3da3-5e33-bb32-277064c4a971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+6I=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533/selection/6846ce3a44439f30e74290b7c4409dc184b0abecbdb785b53e7145cc0bfbaad5" :answer/id #uuid "9db3c4f7-03b7-57ad-aa7b-c329ac6f1625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+18I=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533/selection/93f2b7d9b5e8acd5cd3cee3005c87a3f719b4da5a2fe7a1be8ceaf0f9b3df9e5" :answer/id #uuid "f36855c0-ec78-5eda-aef0-9a855f752f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-6I=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7b8cf85-a8f5-5221-8a53-db19ef2c1c3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-336533/selection/b584697703567f8b802de003bcc741885eed27ee25f4f9483d253ce765801b6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336533/selection/9111e286e028a3b1572db98fcd1243c12bef07f305596b311cec8f8a0f454bc2" "q-336533/selection/c6e9e1786651e68e47bfd6d8dfa488215d83d8471885336cc662bd783796c744" "q-336533/selection/b584697703567f8b802de003bcc741885eed27ee25f4f9483d253ce765801b6c" "q-336533/selection/6846ce3a44439f30e74290b7c4409dc184b0abecbdb785b53e7145cc0bfbaad5" "q-336533/selection/93f2b7d9b5e8acd5cd3cee3005c87a3f719b4da5a2fe7a1be8ceaf0f9b3df9e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336533" :question/id #uuid "5db08a12-2bed-5c19-bee6-fdb879966b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-336533" :question/problem "A series RL circuit has a source electromotive force (EMF) of $6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistance of $18\\,Ω,$ and an inductance of $3\\,\\text{H}.$ Find the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ (in amperes) in the circuit at time $t$ (in seconds)." :question/worked-solution "Kirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RL circuit, there are two voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=18\\,Ω.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=18I\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=3\\,\\text{H}.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ in the circuit is\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)=18I+3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dI}{dt}+6I=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336533/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11687da5-3a8e-56cb-adec-e3fa5cadf490"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336533"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection/8f22a6d6a51318bb5dafefb7c66c23d197caa6e7e47662df134e6fd3a6d8fef3" :answer/id #uuid "303ff0a0-bb18-51b4-b5f5-072e815529b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+3I=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection/f029fcd005104e12d41d50e9861d30e531cd8ed5992f19b26882d7964ddaeddc" :answer/id #uuid "e2c37afc-a0a4-5da0-8af0-e8c68c2ef928" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+9I=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection/e2462d29c22ba4bf7924318812d9547b05b83b12daa39fac1158bf2c633f6da3" :answer/id #uuid "a2693c51-9dd7-5198-9998-228ef866fb1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+3I=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection/18c0736eb679b35152a2d24617689c098b1e1c0502f50014e78b4d03478a13c4" :answer/id #uuid "75f927f6-5546-5042-a7a2-7f2fcbed89a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-3I=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection/8306dece0cedec8b75f8a408e547b77f5e7358503c505a7d7beeb5d2c4102e7d" :answer/id #uuid "48ac7453-72f7-56c7-8a3e-2fdcbb34cdd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-9I=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dfe6fcf-ee28-5baa-beef-def0b1219075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-336546/selection/e2462d29c22ba4bf7924318812d9547b05b83b12daa39fac1158bf2c633f6da3" :answer-field/choices ["q-336546/selection/8f22a6d6a51318bb5dafefb7c66c23d197caa6e7e47662df134e6fd3a6d8fef3" "q-336546/selection/f029fcd005104e12d41d50e9861d30e531cd8ed5992f19b26882d7964ddaeddc" "q-336546/selection/e2462d29c22ba4bf7924318812d9547b05b83b12daa39fac1158bf2c633f6da3" "q-336546/selection/18c0736eb679b35152a2d24617689c098b1e1c0502f50014e78b4d03478a13c4" "q-336546/selection/8306dece0cedec8b75f8a408e547b77f5e7358503c505a7d7beeb5d2c4102e7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336546" :question/id #uuid "38df6533-3590-5853-a74e-af1a3c2be976" :question/math-academy-id "q-336546" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043558/assets/999acaa0bc014b7afc7c916dd03c957e15707ca680836341e5a071a1f321e97d.png)\n\nFind the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ (in amperes) at time $t$ (in seconds) in the circuit given in the diagram above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows a series RL circuit with a source electromotive force (EMF) of $E(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistor with resistance $9\\,Ω,$ and an inductor with an inductance of $3\\,\\text{H}.$\n\nKirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RL circuit, there are two voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=9\\,Ω.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=9I\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=3\\,\\text{H}.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ in the circuit is\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)=9I+3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dI}{dt}+3I=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336546/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11687da5-3a8e-56cb-adec-e3fa5cadf490"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336542/selection/1ffeedf9c6226ade7e9fec9eb7a573902ed7a8eb525c1468cc6a478bb90373b4" :answer/id #uuid "d8ea85da-aa8c-5c1f-be7e-96677cc036d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+6I=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336542/selection/6f1e04e487f5678c6f2a4ab7939a58ee9f43ecdfd9d74f8dccc3b334d5ec468e" :answer/id #uuid "6a1da50b-0f87-55ec-a82f-32d041402416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-6I=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336542/se