shows a series RL circuit with a source electromotive force (EMF) of $6\\,\\text{V},$ a resistor with resistance $18\\,Ω,$ and an inductor with an inductance of $3\\,\\text{H}.$\n\nKirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RL circuit, there are two voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=18\\,Ω.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=18I\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=3\\,\\text{H}.$\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, the differential equation governing the amount of current $I$ in the circuit is\n\n$$\n6=18I+3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dI}{dt}+6I=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11687da5-3a8e-56cb-adec-e3fa5cadf490"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336543/selection/b7e2b0b1d840006613645d17b3e42b468c385a81e9a63fe9a69491c0066d62d9" :answer/id #uuid "7cd4f528-0d65-5038-83d1-f281ed18cac8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-16I=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336543/selection/267cd0ebc4e5134c9d9a2b33605317dbfca286937893b9d0d37fee11ace2a339" :answer/id #uuid "37a43329-d36d-5ae7-bdea-82c73bf260a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}-4I=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336543/selection/1c7151c36ce3e7588d1da0a827145c59a3a52d1e2084d3836b84fc336563dfbe" :answer/id #uuid "884a5272-27a3-5d57-9466-5e634f196ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dI}{dt}+4I=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336543/selection/86a261642a835fe3e8a02ce5d8fa9917952b5611a0109fb4171278c05